descriere:
Nivel de vechime: Nivel mediu de experiență
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Servicii IT și consultanță IT și Instruire și asistență pentru sisteme IT
Job Responsibilities 
 Responsible for on-site desktop operations and support in Romania, including the installation, configuration, troubleshooting, and routine maintenance of office terminals, peripherals, and on-site IT equipment;
 Responsible for the full lifecycle management of IT hardware assets, covering asset receipt, registration, inventory, transfer, repair, and disposal, to ensure consistency between records and physical assets;
 Establish and maintain hardware asset ledgers, regularly produce asset inventory reports, and assist in completing internal and external asset audits;
 Responsible for spare parts management for on-site hardware equipment and liaison with suppliers, coordinating equipment repair and replacement;
 Respond to service requests from on-site users, process tickets promptly in accordance with SLA requirements, and ensure business continuity on site;
 Collaborate with the remote operations team to complete on-site and remote operations tasks, and promptly report major on-site issues;
 Complete other on-site operations support tasks assigned by superiors.
 Requirements 
 Practical experience in on-site desktop support (Desktop Support), with familiarity with Windows office environments, commonly used office software, and peripheral maintenance;
 Must have experience in IT hardware asset management and be familiar with the identification, configuration, and management of hardware assets (servers, PCs, printers, network equipment, etc.)—this is a mandatory requirement;
 Able to work on-site in Romania for an extended period and accept overseas assignment arrangements;
 Good service awareness and communication skills, with the ability to independently handle on-site emergencies;
 Conscientious and detail-oriented, with a strong sense of responsibility and execution.
 Priority Conditions 
 Familiarity with ITIL operations and maintenance processes and relevant certifications (e.g., ITIL, CompTIA A+) are preferred.
